From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 05:43:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Stop allocating on the entity-collision, village and goal
 scans

Four independent per-tick allocation sites found by JFR:

EnumDirectionLimit.facings() built a fresh array on every call, and it is
called once per iterator() and once per random(); it now hands out shared
arrays. They live in a holder class because EnumDirection.<clinit> reaches
EnumDirectionLimit.<clinit> through EnumAxis's constants while NORTH..DOWN
are still null - static fields here would silently fill with nulls, so
EnumDirectionFacingsTest pins that down.

Entity.checkBlockCollisions walked every block the bounding box touches and
built a BlockPosition for each, though Block.onEntityCollidedWithBlock is an
empty default that only eleven blocks override. It now skips the position
unless the block declares hasEntityCollisionHandler(). Only the four-argument
override counts - BlockStairs and friends override the three-argument variant,
which this loop never calls.

PersistentVillage.addDoorsAround visits 32*8*32 blocks every tick and keeps
only the doors; PathfinderGoalGotoTarget.searchForDestination scans O(n^3)
candidates and keeps at most one. Both now scan with raw ints (a reused
mutable position in the goal's case) and materialize only what is retained.

Chunk's three horizontal-facing loops are indexed rather than iterated.

Measured over 60s of play: these sites went from 65 MB/min to zero, and no
AxisAlignedBB or CollisionBoxSink regression appeared alongside them.

